From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Melanie Riise <me@mriise.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:30:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [zlib][x86] Check CPU and OS support before AVX-512
 CRC-32

When built with CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL (CMake ENABLE_SIMD_AVX512),
_cpu_check_features() enables the AVX-512 CRC-32 kernel based only on
_xgetbv(0) & 0x40. That check has three problems:

- XGETBV raises #UD unless CPUID reports both XSAVE and OSXSAVE, so
  CPUs or OSes without XSAVE support crash during feature detection.
- CPUID is never asked for AVX-512F or VPCLMULQDQ. AVX-512 CPUs
  without VPCLMULQDQ (e.g. Skylake-X) pass the check and then fault on
  the first 512-bit carry-less multiply.
- XCR0 bit 6 alone does not mean the OS saves the XMM, YMM, opmask
  and Hi16_ZMM state the kernel relies on.

Check XSAVE/OSXSAVE before XGETBV and CPUID leaf 7 availability before
reading it. Then require SSE4.1, SSE4.2 and PCLMULQDQ (used by the
final reduction), SSE2, AVX-512F and VPCLMULQDQ, and XCR0 state bits
1, 2, 5, 6 and 7. The predicate is a static inline function in
cpu_features.h so it can be unit tested without the matching CPU.
The header gains an include guard so the test can include it.

Also use _mm512_zextsi128_si512 for the initial CRC: the upper lanes
of _mm512_castsi128_si512 are undefined, and the kernel XORs the whole
vector into the input.

The GN build does not define CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL, so Chromium's
shipping configuration is unchanged.

Tests: two new ZlibTest cases cover the predicate bit by bit and
compare crc32_z against a bitwise reference for 64 alignments, vector
boundary lengths, four seeds and split updates.

Bug: TODO_FILE_CRBUG
